          <p style="font-family: 'Open Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 0.92rem; color: #555; margin: 0 0 16px;">The small unit. Roughly a one-car garage worth of sealed steel space.</p>

          <div style="overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: 16px;">
            <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.95rem;">
              <tbody>
                <tr><td style="padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5; font-weight: 600; width: 46%;">Dimensions</td><td style="padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5;">20 ft long × 8 ft wide × 8.5 ft tall</td></tr>
                <tr><td style="padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5; font-weight: 600;">Floor space</td><td style="padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5;">~160 sq ft</td></tr>
                <tr><td style="padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5; font-weight: 600;">Total volume</td><td style="padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5;">~1,170 cubic ft</td></tr>
                <tr><td style="padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5; font-weight: 600;">Door opening</td><td style="padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5;">7.7 ft wide × 7.5 ft tall (double doors)</td></tr>
                <tr><td style="padding: 9px 12px; font-weight: 600;">Access</td><td style="padding: 9px 12px;">Drive-up, personal gate code, 24/7</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>What fits:</strong> the contents of a 1–2 bedroom apartment — queen bed, dresser, couch, dining table and chairs, washer/dryer, and 20–30 medium boxes. Also good for tools, ATVs, motorcycles, and small workshop equipment.</p>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 16px;"><strong>Rent this one if:</strong> you're between homes, downsizing, storing seasonal or hunting gear, or you're a trade needing a lockable tool and materials box you can back a truck up to.</p>

